
SELECT salary
FROM (
    SELECT salary,
           DENSE_RANK() OVER (ORDER BY salary DESC) AS rnk
    FROM Employee
) e
WHERE rnk = N;

DENSE_RANK() - assigns the same rank to duplicate salaries and doesn't skip the next rank, so it finds the Nth distinct highest salary."
ROW_NUMBER() - If they instead ask for the Nth employee/row by salary, even when salaries are duplicated, you'd use ROW_NUMBER() instead.

///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

SELECT DISTINCT salary
FROM Employee
ORDER BY salary DESC
LIMIT 1 OFFSET N - 1;

